Hi folks.

We're doing some testing of NAO in preparation for a probable move to
the Amazon EC2 cloud sometime in the next month or two. This will
bring with it many advantages:

1) Continued low latency. Current hosting at hurricane electric
(he.net) is great latency from the San Jose, CA, and good connectivity
elsewhere. This cloud hosting will be from a similar area with
Amazon's infrastructure, so latency should continue to be great.

2) Reliability. Before, if I had a hardware failure, nao was down for
hours or days while I hauled myself to the data center to repair
things. Now it will be a matter of relaunching an EC2 instance.

3) Backup. EC2 provides a way for me to snapshot the backend block
store (EBS). This allows me to take somewhat regular backups at a
block level in addition to the file level backups that I've been
doing.

4) Additional EU location (?). I might end up launching an
eu.nethack.alt.org instance, since EC2 has a cloud location in
Ireland. I've long wanted to put multi-site support in dgamelaunch to
view games from multiple locations, and this may be the way to do it.

5) Security. Having these instances be replicable, etc, allow me to
test new versions of OS, etc in parallel and generally keep up with
security patches more easily than I do now.

6) Cost. This will end up costing me less in the long term. While my
monthly charges will probably be similar for now, the fact that I
don't have to worry about hardware cost will make this less expensive
in the long term. Doesn't help you any, but helps me take less flak
from the wife for hosting nao.

What I need now, is some people to play with the ec2 instance nao, and
give me feedback on latency. (or give paxed feedback on #nethack on
freenode) aws1.alt.org is a copy of nao as of yesterday, and should
function with saves/accounts from then.

Please telnet to aws1.alt.org, and give it a go. I'm primarily
interested in feedback on latency, stalls (if any), and the overall
interactive experience compared to the current nao. Note that this is
a throwaway test instance so high scores/saves/etc won't be kept and
aren't reflected on alt.org.

telnet://aws1.alt.org

